<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal" spacebelow="2" spaceabove="8"><Font executable="false">State-Space Variables</Font></Text-field></Title>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal" spacebelow="3" spaceabove="3"><Font executable="false">The chosen states should at least include the generalized coordinates and their first-time derivatives.</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal" spacebelow="3" spaceabove="3"><Font executable="false">X is the state vector.</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal" spacebelow="3" spaceabove="3"><Font executable="false">In the state vector X: Lagrangian coordinates are first, followed by their first-time derivatives, and finally any other states, as required.</Font></Text-field>
<Group labelreference="L20" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">Substitution sets for the states (to obtain time-independent state equations).</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs_Xq := { seq( q[i] = X[i], i=1..Nq ) };
subs_Xqd := { seq( qd[i] = X[i+Nq], i=1..Nq ) };</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">PCQvLSZJInhHNiI2IyIiIjYjSSJ0R0YnJkkiWEdGJ0YoLy0mRiY2IyIiI0YqJkYtRjE=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">PCQvLUklZGlmZkclKnByb3RlY3RlZEc2JC0mSSJ4RzYiNiMiIiI2I0kidEdGK0YvJkkiWEdGKzYjIiIkLy1GJTYkLSZGKjYjIiIjRi5GLyZGMTYjIiIl</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L21" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">Substitution set for the input(s).</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">set the input to be the current cmd to the two motors and gravity</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs_U := { ud = U[1],F[c]=U[2],g=U[3]};</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">PCUvSSJnRzYiJkkiVUdGJTYjIiIkLyZJIkZHRiU2I0kiY0dGJSZGJzYjIiIjLy1JJWRpZmZHJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHNiQtJkkiekdGJTYjSSJyR0YlNiNJInRHRiVGPSZGJzYjIiIi</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L22" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">Nu = number of inputs; U = input (row) vector (e.g. U = [ V[m] ] )</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Nu := nops( subs_U );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">IiIk</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L23" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">substitution set for the position states' second time derivatives</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs_Xqdd := { seq( diff( q[i], t$2 ) =  Xd[i+Nq], i=1..Nq ) };</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">PCQvLUklZGlmZkclKnByb3RlY3RlZEc2JC1GJTYkLSZJInhHNiI2IyIiIjYjSSJ0R0YtRjFGMSZJI1hkR0YtNiMiIiQvLUYlNiQtRiU2JC0mRiw2IyIiI0YwRjFGMSZGMzYjIiIl</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L24" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">second time derivatives of the position states (written as time-independent variables).</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">The set of unknowns is obtained from this list to solve the Lagrange's equations of motion.</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Xqdd := [ seq( Xd[i+Nq], i=1..Nq ) ];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">NyQmSSNYZEc2IjYjIiIkJkYkNiMiIiU=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L25" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">substitution set to linearize the state-space matrices (i.e. A and B) </Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">about the quiescent null state vector (small-displacement theory)</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs_XUzero := { seq( X[i] = 0, i=1..2*Nq ), seq( U[i] = 0, i=1..Nu ) };</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">PCkvJkkiVUc2IjYjIiIiIiIhLyZGJTYjIiIjRikvJkYlNiMiIiRGKS8mSSJYR0YmRidGKS8mRjRGLEYpLyZGNEYwRikvJkY0NiMiIiVGKQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L26" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">Nx = dim( X ) = total number of states (should be greater than or equal to: 2 * Nq)</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">Ny = chosen number of outputs</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L27" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Nx := 2 * Nq + 0:
Ny := Nq:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
</Section>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal" spacebelow="4" spaceabove="8"><Font executable="false">Total Potential and Kinetic Energies of the System</Font></Text-field></Title>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">The total potential and kinetic energies are needed to calculate the Lagrangian of the system.</Font></Text-field>
<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spacebelow="2" spaceabove="8"><Font style="2D Input" executable="false">Total Potential Energy: </Font><Equation executable="false" style="2D Comment" input-equation="">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2I1EhRictRiM2I0YrRis=</Equation><Font style="2D Input" executable="false"> </Font></Text-field></Title>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">The total potential energy can be expressed in terms of the generalized coordinates alone.</Font></Text-field>
