<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal" spacebelow="2" spaceabove="8"><Font executable="false">Additional Insight: Inertia (or mass) Matrix: Fi</Font></Text-field></Title>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">The nonlinear system of equations resulting from the Lagrangian mechanics can be written in the following matrix form:</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">F( q ) . qdd + G( q, qd ) . qd + H( q ) . q = L( q, qd, u )</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">F, G, and H are called, respectively, the mass, damping, and stiffness matrices.</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">They are symmetric in form.</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">The inertia (a.k.a. mass) matrix, F, gives indications regarding the coupling existing in the system.</Font></Text-field>
<Group labelreference="L63" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Fi := Matrix( Nq, Nq ):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L64" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">for i from 1 to Nq do
  for k from 1 to Nq do
    Fi[ i, k ] := simplify( diff( op( 1, EOM_states[i] ), Xd[k+Nq] ) );
    Fi[ i, k ] := collect( combine( Fi[ i, k ], trig ), cos );
  end do;
end do:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L65" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="2D Input" executable="false" layout="Normal"><Font executable="false">Here, Fi shows a linear system</Font></Text-field>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">'F[i]' = Fi;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LyZJIkZHNiI2I0kiaUdGJS1JJ01hdHJpeEc2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJTYjL0kkJWlkR0YlIik7ZFolKQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
</Section>
